{
  "name": "Assassin's Blood (Ingested)",
  "type": "consumable",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A creature subjected to this poison must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 6 (1d12) poison damage and is @Compendium[dnd5e.rules.w7eitkpD7QQTB6j0]{poisoned} for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't @Compendium[dnd5e.rules.w7eitkpD7QQTB6j0]{poisoned}.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Ingested.</strong></em> A creature must swallow an entire dose of ingested poison to suffer its effects. The dose can be delivered in food or a liquid. You may decide that a partial dose has a reduced effect, such as allowing advantage on the saving throw or dealing only half damage on a failed save.</p>",
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "Gear"
    },
